# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source .` tars up and uploads to the
# Cloud Build staging bucket - a SEPARATE step from the Docker build itself
# (.dockerignore controls that, once the tarball already exists). Without
# this file, gcloud has no local .gitignore to fall back on (there isn't
# one in this directory - only one at the repo root, which gcloud doesn't
# walk up to), so it uploads everything, including output/ - this app's
# local Street View/Vision image cache, which can grow to gigabytes after
# repeated local runs. That's the actual cause of a deploy appearing to
# hang at "Uploading sources..." for a very long time on an otherwise fast
# connection: it isn't stuck, it's re-uploading the entire local cache on
# every single deploy. Keep this in sync with .dockerignore - they serve
# different stages but should exclude the same things.
output/
precision_sample_output/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore
*.venv/
venv/
keys.env
keys.env.example
README.md
